{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Allow the creation of global BBC iPlayer for international audiences",
        "additional_details": "The Government is deciding the BBC\u2019s future now. The Charter Review sets the framework to 2038. On iPlayer: millions already use VPNs to access BBC content; charging \u00a35\u20138/month could unlock major new revenue. \r\n \r\nIn 2024, it was reported the number of BritBox International (BBC) subscribers grew by 300%, with nearly 4m subscribers. We believe the BBC has strong global appeal in children and nature content.",
        "background": "We believe we should prioritise commercial growth over cuts. We feel BBC dramas, documentaries and children\u2019s programmes are some of the best and appeal to global audiences. Millions bypass geo-blocks to watch them. We call on the Government to allow a global BBC iPlayer.",
